alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson to 3.1.0 instead of the 2.9.4 I first chose, because the reviewer rejected the 2.9.4 commit and asked for 3.1.0. The PR is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`. The name is outdated, since the content pins 3.1.0. I left it as is.\n- **Changes:** `requirements.txt` moves `fastjson==2.8.0` to `fastjson==3.1.0`, and `CHANGELOG.md` gets an entry under Unreleased.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on commit `597dec07c7`.\n- **PR:** #101, \"Upgrade fastjson to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337\". The first open request timed out, so I checked the PR list before retrying and found it had been created. I then added alex as a reviewer.\n- **Code impact:** nothing in `src/` or the tests uses fastjson, so the code path is unaffected. Moving from 2.x to 3.x is a major-version change, so alex should check the dependency's release notes for breaking changes even though CI passed.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}